diffs.patch:
Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/ca-clients.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/ca-clients.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/ca-clients.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:d69cec38183c409bf7a594bf8b63b7f69260d8a9705ed4442b70b2c99ef0e1e2",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_794319e2e009432b9eecdefad3dc7169",
+      "statement": "All certificate-related commands talk to a CA through the CaClient interface in utils/cautils/client.go, which covers X.509 sign/renew/revoke/rekey, SSH sign/renew/rekey/revoke/roots/federation/config/check-host/hosts/bastion, version probing, root pool access, and CA URL access.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L27-L48",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d9082e3dc6bfd7f7ef4fda03bbc2077610af0366eb8e8085ee0b4043dd65958:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5399625c36da422bb4acdddae2af763d",
+      "statement": "cautils.NewClient returns an in-process OfflineCA when --offline is set (requiring --ca-config) and otherwise builds an online client via ca.NewClient with ca.WithRootFile(root), where root defaults to pki.GetRootCAPath().",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L52-L74",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:728e02c9fda0397f940ca7b0af3633c0e94b12b6a90ea0c7f7b0dbc4d00b5619:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_1ea1ffb1231b418cb26b5e3ce073a1f1",
+      "statement": "NewAdminClient authenticates against the step-ca Admin API using --admin-cert/--admin-key when provided, otherwise it generates an ephemeral admin identity by minting a SignType token, creating a CSR, calling client.Sign, and passing the result via ca.WithAdminX5C.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L99-L204",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:966317c783e03925080050b58d8f80d6abb517cba0e23d1709518f4ecfac2b58:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7c2179fa416c4681b134f245c25e8b28",
+      "statement": "CertificateFlow.GetClient trusts the CA from a token's sha claim and http audience using ca.WithRootSHA256, deriving the CA URL from the token audience when --ca-url is absent; otherwise it requires --ca-url and --root (or the default root path).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L134-L171",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eac06e54a30b1c44b73cef0ba05ec80a593dabe45011372e61bc7bd15ba6eeb7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f02a5e2cb65b475c904eae11daa48448",
+      "statement": "OfflineCA is a process-wide singleton wrapping the smallstep/certificates authority.Authority, built from the ca.json configuration, to avoid double initialization because backends such as badgerDB take locks on open.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L36-L81",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:535a7ad7ebf3f401a29b0c771c81fe1d6113871042646acb5be94508de7544d1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_73c3a1adc83b4c26bbc1ccec5eeb77af",
+      "statement": "OfflineCA Sign runs authority.Authorize followed by authority.SignWithContext; Revoke builds authority.RevokeOptions from a token (MTLS=false) or the client certificate extracted from the passed *http.Transport (MTLS=true); Renew and Rekey extract the peer certificate from TLSClientConfig.Certificates[0].",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L196-L222",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7ea102fb32e8b0b3f3d4c5a4e7f27f9edfbdc4d295484002cbfcb641ddc2fa5:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L277-L341",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0f79ed48611a4e5dfd7904cf3331d40bfed187a05d108d0f550f0aca0775d5d1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_933926cb88f6431685f4cd843f65da63",
+      "statement": "The renewer in command/ca/renew.go builds its own http.Transport with a root pool and (while the certificate is valid) an mTLS client certificate, then creates the online client with ca.NewClient(caURL, ca.WithTransport(tr)) or falls back to cautils.NewOfflineCA under --offline.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L425-L480",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33a946aa7797b12818ee4247cbe7f3f5ea0f6174ea66a69cec015ff70832392f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-08-31T04:41:54.708Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/environment-and-contexts.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/environment-and-contexts.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/environment-and-contexts.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:4d955dfdb400ce494ad6a5479cb24f3127237ad1dd063eb27cc62c8cc8713e56",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6f795cdda79b4d208f68e00a80747f29",
+      "statement": "The base step path defaults to $HOME/.step, is overridable via STEPPATH, and is printed by `step path --base`; `step path` resolves to the current authority path and `step path --profile` to the current profile base path.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/path/path.go#L92-L104",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00cdca980003829a7447155b2741a8cf3ef9051ed879f2ad911fd001e60d64e8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_df6a4a6fe6eb48018fd71ebc59a2326b",
+      "statement": "step ca bootstrap downloads the root certificate into pki.GetRootCAPath() under the step path and writes config/defaults.json containing ca-url, fingerprint, root, and optional redirect-url/provisioner/min-password-length fields so later commands can omit --ca-url/--root/--fingerprint.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L145-L193",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09195a92186178806f3650fa29dc229604efea82dd433c20edddaf0e13c550b6:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d274bc510ee6428f87d15acd7987ab20",
+      "statement": "UseContext returns true when context management is enabled or when any of --context, --authority, or --profile is set, and context-creating commands (ca init, ca bootstrap) call step.Contexts().Add, SaveCurrent, and SetCurrent.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L37-L42",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f23f01b95e618bdb13f019cfc7f1685162cdf994cb27eb36fa4811fff8e1154f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_91a80b951e444894bbd4b765d07e0e4b",
+      "statement": "step context remove refuses to remove the current context, skips deleting an authority or profile directory still referenced by another context, asks for confirmation without --force, and always removes the SSH includes line associated with the removed authority.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/context/remove.go#L47-L118",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9745255d8143a8ac4f0d7ae005476f86c0aef7674285955ee2f19c8b7334a420:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_50f063934ed84e909246f3f4236bde7f",
+      "statement": "step context select persists the default context via step.Contexts().SaveCurrent, and step context current prints the selected context name or a JSON object with name, authority, and profile when --json is passed.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/context/current.go#L46-L69",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f103243ba9ad0918792aeb57ed33273fbfc1e09b774b92c282e5692d3f63af18:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/context/select.go#L34-L43",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:212eb7363f73cb8d2da6806190a8cc875d70e27ca48ac2e58ad3a1e0347116c1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9c3ba1c032504a8a838194cd5f6747b9",
+      "statement": "step ca init creates a context when UseContext is true, defaulting the context, authority, and profile names to the first DNS name of the new CA when their flags are not set.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/init.go#L544-L570",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b3fcd12aa8a4b6a0ba5c59a536223c5954f3666895ac4c09e1ee49dd4fca318:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_64037e114453411faab9f815c4f10558",
+      "statement": "When contexts are enabled, bootstrap ensures a profiles/<profile> defaults file exists, writing an empty JSON object when the file is absent.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L197-L210",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd0525574d4d23a4ef560e8abf9b7cf01e1ddc6e34a15cd970ce491d66391510:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fa4909af9a3d48e38da1e08ab969852f",
+      "statement": "If an existing CA configuration is present at config/ca.json while not using contexts, WarnContext advises the user to adopt contexts; the step context command help documents the contexts.json shape as a map of name to {authority, profile}.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/context/context.go#L21-L36",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:948ae856fb2fff05f7475e74efe674ffd2fc901fe9879530fb611501705c7eca:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/bootstrap.go#L49-L54",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f346221be88b93dac6178f11103f261807509086083d0ce164f4db376e064aa4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-08-31T04:41:54.708Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/concepts/tokens-and-provisioners.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/concepts/tokens-and-provisioners.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/concepts/tokens-and-provisioners.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:54ed872cbf36378eb23e10b8d4bc0d8af8fadfe6404f8974fc9add767dbd5af1",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6a64bcce120b4b76806becd636990611",
+      "statement": "Default token claims use issuer step-cli, audience https://ca/sign, and a 5 minute default validity, with validity bounded between 10 seconds and 1 hour and a maximum 30 minute delay before validity starts.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/token.go#L11-L24",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e8f611f0b655155c2b0161387c2838bad216d0b53e910180096bf75f2c1671a:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/token.go#L117-L130",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c2734c9d11850ffab88536b9f8428d0ca6017e99abb8c181587d19e8b6d61e24:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_697d265d7df9480399af698eac399e4c",
+      "statement": "Claims.Sign adds a kid header computed as the SHA-256 thumbprint of the signing key, forces the aud claim to a string for single-element audiences, and serializes the JWT in compact form.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/token.go#L70-L104",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e172a43f85107bddab7ba8baab6e4ff0505bf0bb98f19f498e6a948da4989ba2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_cf332702e8a74ab39d916b44b2019de1",
+      "statement": "WithConfirmationFingerprint and WithFingerprint set a cnf claim with x5rt#S256, binding the token to a CSR, SSH public key, or fingerprint as Proof-of-Possession.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/options.go#L110-L144",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79e4c1087dca41343b8d7dc54919224cd828df9a6a58907ce99adced41605d6b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_00bee8c2884a4005a9868338251fc191",
+      "statement": "Payload.Type classifies tokens as JWK, X5C, OIDC, GCP, AWS, Azure, K8sSA, Nebula, or Unknown from claims (google/amazon claims, kubernetes/serviceaccount issuer, sha/sans claims), with ParseInsecure used by commands that defer validation to the CA.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/parse.go#L153-L189",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d7e7fcd2292450a83ffa8d9b96ee016b39f598253f75ad8975adc385e667763:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/parse.go#L64-L82",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b6ded519c51e95ec8a89abd9b5278db5b992b3775542cb82177ce0861501abe1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0172caa749c848f382addab14281790c",
+      "statement": "parseAudience derives the token audience from the CA URL and token type, appending /1.0/sign, /1.0/renew, /1.0/revoke, /1.0/ssh/sign, /1.0/ssh/renew, /1.0/ssh/revoke, or /1.0/ssh/rekey.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L39-L76",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31e0d37473f0678195165f95e9d89e97299cfd46c98ebdc66157984630f16460:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_46ee23ac8baf461fbc551316eee4fe99",
+      "statement": "NewTokenFlow fetches the provisioner list from the CA, filters and prompts for a provisioner, and dispatches token generation by provisioner type (JWK, OIDC, X5C, Nebula, SSHPOP, K8sSA, GCP, AWS, Azure, ACME, SCEP), short-circuiting renew tokens to generateRenewToken.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L101-L183",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a206beb644478060eeb535b0495937c744cf645f516ffc3684fa13fa81394d6d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_949c6f92d4d64d2a94f345f5d3477ceb",
+      "statement": "loadJWK loads the signing key from --key/KMS or decrypts the provisioner's encrypted key fetched from the CA via pki.GetProvisionerKey, using the provisioner's kid as the JWT kid.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_generator.go#L380-L439",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dccc9d7ba4d89aa747afc518bdde5b47596c88e98b7ff5e0c5b9caaf9612898a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_dddffa1d79cb418a98b37f16cc233f93",
+      "statement": "generateOIDCToken invokes `step oauth --oidc --bare` with the provisioner's configuration endpoint, client id/secret, scopes, auth params, listen address, and console flag to obtain the OIDC identity token.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_generator.go#L144-L169",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b8fc1a4ae7b27158b6d8bb033718a63281a9afe422fc46eac7a4db4b19ffd47:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_17c5ef0501b8471a94ea1fdb969f64a9",
+      "statement": "OfflineTokenFlow delegates to OfflineCA.GenerateToken when ca.json exists, otherwise requires --provisioner/--issuer and --key and builds a JWK or X5C token directly with kid from --kid or the key thumbprint.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L212-L273",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e5545ce9d5f6f123130d7bb8540c83843366521759f35c9f488b0fd721c4ed4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_253702760639421e9370da5b301d22f7",
+      "statement": "step ca token maps --revoke/--renew/--rekey and --ssh/--host/--principal flags to token types, adds confirmation claims from --cnf/--cnf-file, parses validity bounds, and writes the token to --output-file with mode 0600.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/token.go#L303-L443",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76dd5e9922de21131c28eb81d6338bf8b58c276f99e2f0b5564227eb6240d171:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-08-31T04:41:54.708Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/integrations/admin-api.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/integrations/admin-api.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/integrations/admin-api.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:18e03cb2ac3b674bbb3b02e684e6ace5c34fe12613a5766ba8458f1e8649400d",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8c83d2a304c64cf6b0b61a7ee061947c",
+      "statement": "step ca provisioner manages provisioners (list, jwe-key, add, update, remove, webhook) across types JWK, OIDC, AWS, GCP, Azure, ACME, X5C, K8SSA, SSHPOP, SCEP, and Nebula, using linkedca objects through the Admin API.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/provisioner/provisioner.go#L26-L96",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0f93dd527b4517cae054b0c2b02c8d9879b96d1c4614d8d302f8dfbe74a391d5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_004504a5d15c4da89914466f7d66dd71",
+      "statement": "newCRUDClient probes the Admin API with an unauthenticated client: it falls back to editing ca.json via newCaConfigClient on network errors or ca.ErrAdminAPINotImplemented, and falls through to cautils.NewAdminClient on ca.ErrAdminAPINotAuthorized.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/provisioner/provisioner.go#L105-L132",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e9c18cb0ead88711d52c3a493e98126e04c650b9f9e8d233080fd350f6d62de:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_96b79ff7f12e4101bb8783decd04a6e4",
+      "statement": "The ca.json fallback builds an in-process authority from the config with a noop admin DB (nodb) and SkipValidation, and persists every change by saving the provisioner list back to ca.json, printing that step-ca must be restarted or sent SIGHUP.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/provisioner/caConfigClient.go#L207-L220",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:077b546dcbc8c2b2c02ba649623b9befc12a70a9dceeeec31519df3674aa0bb3:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/provisioner/caConfigClient.go#L82-L106",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:96ee334bfa8058c1ca19da530c9fb1aa30a6b764143c9a10ae531858dc99b3f5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0c5bffa066524a61989440899b64c253",
+      "statement": "cautils.NewAdminClient uses --admin-cert/--admin-key when provided and otherwise generates an ephemeral admin identity by minting a SignType token, creating a key and CSR, calling client.Sign, and using the chain with ca.WithAdminX5C.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L99-L204",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:966317c783e03925080050b58d8f80d6abb517cba0e23d1709518f4ecfac2b58:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_244b4199500b449a9ab63179f87a6c07",
+      "statement": "Admin commands filter and select admins by subject and --provisioner through adminPrompt, auto-selecting a single candidate or presenting an interactive ui.Select list enriched with each admin's provisioner name and type.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/admin/admin.go#L96-L151",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cdcc80371a98e45ff6ecfaf3c98939b9b3770e485f5c486b7f02967e795b76c9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4b54912afe3947209723212818e09484",
+      "statement": "step ca policy exposes authority, provisioner, and acme subcommands for managing certificate issuance policies.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/policy/policy.go#L14-L26",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5b24cf1435b6a89524f2b89a789e4d2ec173378445a7a1d663f81835988cb6d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d1b292df54be45409adda9e8e0d1730d",
+      "statement": "step ca provisioner list does not use the Admin API; it calls pki.GetProvisioners(caURL, root) against the public endpoint and prints the JSON provisioner list.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/provisioner/list.go#L40-L63",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:afa6f1c9df762186fbab81075b1d3db4a85cc7152bca525679fbe5a9c7850b63:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6c985dce1dc74c86b1eb248cb8d8b8f8",
+      "statement": "Webhook management requires the Admin API: its newCRUDClient returns an error when a config file exists but the admin API is not enabled, and otherwise builds cautils.NewAdminClient.",
+      "evidence": [
